Id: cont004w
Severity: WARN
Category: containers
Check: check_containers
Fix: Remove --privileged; add only the capability or device the container needs.
References: docker-run(1) --privileged
Controls: CIS 4.1, 5.4; NIST AC-6, CM-7; ISO 8.2, 8.9; CE Secure configuration, User access control

A running container is privileged (--privileged, privileged: true in
compose), or has been given CAP_SYS_ADMIN or every capability. Such a
container can mount the host's disks, load kernel modules and reach
every device: a process that breaks into it, or a root user inside it,
controls the host. Some tools need it (Docker in Docker, some hardware
agents); most containers that have it do not.

To fix it, remove --privileged and grant only what the container needs:
one capability with --cap-add, one device with --device.
